        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:42:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66279,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "<p>Genital lentigines are the most common gynaecological manifestation {26130139}. Ovarian lesions, myxoid uterine leiomyoma, atypical mesenchymal neoplasm of the cervix, vulvar blue naevus, and vulvar myxoma have been reported {11095480; 21934476; 23327071; 6578600; 9415461; 11737445}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:43:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66280,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>Genital lentigines, vulvar myxoma, follicular cysts, cystic teratomas, and serous cystadenomas are usually asymptomatic {11737445; 11095480; 26130139}. The cutaneous and mucosal lentigines/lesions are small. Reported symptoms and signs are variable and depend on the lesion {23327071; 21934476; 9415461; 11737445}. Leiomyomas with myxoid change can be encountered {11737445; 11095480; 23327071; 21934476; 9415461}. Full criteria for diagnosis have been developed {26130139}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:44:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66281,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "<p>CNC is rare, with an unknown prevalence {26130139}. Its gynaecological manifestations are usually found at a young age {11737445; 11095480; 21934476; 23327071; 26130139}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:44:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66282,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "<p>CNC is usually inherited in an autosomal dominant manner, but it can occur de&nbsp;novo. Most cases are due to a germline mutation in the <em>PRKAR1A</em> gene (located on chromosome&nbsp;17q) {26130139}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:44:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66283,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p><em>PRKAR1A</em> defects lead to an increased cell proliferation in cAMP-responsive tissues and tumour formation {26130139}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:44:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66284,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is nonspecific.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:42:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66285,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All the reported lesions have shown histological features compatible with their histotypes {11737445; 11095480; 21934476; 23327071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:42:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66286,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:42:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66287,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The identification of a pathogenic germline mutation of the <em>PRKAR1A</em> gene helps confirm the diagnosis, although such a mutation may be absent in 20&ndash;30% of cases {26130139; 20301463}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:42:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66288,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 469,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> either two major criteria or one major criterion and one supplemental one.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-16T12:45:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
